msgid ""
"Each person authorised to provide key material for a GDHCN Participant has a"
" GPG key, named in the Letter of Application. The key SHALL be compliant "
"with RFC 4880 (OpenPGP), as the Letter of Application requires, and SHALL "
"meet the following:"
msgstr ""
"Chaque personne autorisée à fournir du matériel cryptographique pour un "
"participant au GDHCN dispose d’une clé GPG, mentionnée dans la lettre de "
"candidature. La clé DOIT être conforme à la RFC 4880 (OpenPGP), comme "
"l’exige la lettre de candidature, et DOIT satisfaire aux conditions "
"suivantes :"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L188
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:188
msgid "EC (e.g. ECDSA)"
msgstr "EC (par exemple ECDSA)"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L59
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:59
msgid ""
"Every GDHCN Participant's Backend can provide their own TLS certificate. "
"This certificate will be whitelisted explicitly and thus may be issued by a "
"publicly trusted certificate authority (e.g. a certificate authority that "
"follows the baseline requirements of the CA Browser forum), by a "
"jurisdictional certificate authority or it can be self-signed. Every GDHCN "
"Participant is responsible for their jurisdictional data and the protection "
"of the private key used to establish the connection to the TNG. Clearly, the"
" “bring your own certificate” approach requires a well-defined registration "
"and identification process as well as revocation and renewal procedures that"
" are described in Section \"Registration of GDHCN Participant Backends\"."
msgstr ""
"Chaque système dorsal de participant au GDHCN peut fournir son propre "
"certificat TLS. Ce certificat sera explicitement inscrit sur liste blanche "
"et peut donc être émis par une autorité de certification publiquement "
"reconnue (par exemple une autorité de certification qui suit les exigences "
"de base du CA/Browser Forum), par une autorité de certification relevant de "
"la juridiction, ou être auto-signé. Chaque participant au GDHCN est "
"responsable des données relevant de sa juridiction et de la protection de la"
" clé privée utilisée pour établir la connexion avec la TNG. De toute "
"évidence, l’approche consistant à « apporter son propre certificat » exige "
"un processus d’enregistrement et d’identification bien défini ainsi que des "
"procédures de révocation et de renouvellement, qui sont décrits à la section"
" « Enregistrement des systèmes dorsaux des participants au GDHCN »."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md#L132
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-
#. trust/concepts_certificate_governance.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_certificate_governance.md:132
msgid ""
"Expired certificates SHALL be removed from the whitelist and trust list."
msgstr ""
"Les certificats expirés DOIVENT être retirés de la liste blanche et de la "
"liste de confiance."

