#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L111
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L116
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:111 input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:116
msgid "DDCC FHIR Implementation Guide"
msgstr "Guide de mise en œuvre FHIR des DDCC"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L115
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:115
msgid ""
"DDCC Vaccination Status (DDCC:TR) documents the use cases, data "
"requirements, technical specifications and implementation guidance for "
"vaccination certificates."
msgstr ""
"Statut vaccinal DDCC (DDCC:TR) documente les cas d’utilisation, les "
"exigences en matière de données, les spécifications techniques et les "
"orientations pour la mise en œuvre relatives aux certificats de vaccination."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L110
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:110
msgid ""
"DDCC Vaccination Status (DDCC:VS) documents the use cases, data "
"requirements, technical specifications and implementation guidance for "
"vaccination certificates."
msgstr ""
"Statut vaccinal DDCC (DDCC:VS) documente les cas d’utilisation, les "
"exigences en matière de données, les spécifications techniques et les "
"orientations pour la mise en œuvre relatives aux certificats de vaccination."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L70
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:70
msgid ""
"Due to the shortening of the identifier (for space-preserving reasons) there"
" is a slim but non-zero chance that the overall list of DSCs accepted by a "
"validator may contain DSCs with duplicate s. For this reason, a verifier "
"MUST check all DSCs with that ."
msgstr ""
"En raison du raccourcissement de l’identifiant (pour des raisons d’économie "
"d’espace), il existe une probabilité faible mais non nulle que la liste "
"globale des DSC acceptés par un validateur contienne des DSC ayant des s en "
"double. Pour cette raison, un vérificateur DOIT contrôler tous les DSC ayant"
" ce ."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L213
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:213
msgid ""
"Each participant is ultimately responsible for compiling their own master "
"list and making that available to the other Participants. The aid of GDHCN's"
" Secretariat for coordinating operational and practical matters is "
"available."
msgstr ""
"Chaque participant est en dernier ressort responsable de la compilation de "
"sa propre liste maîtresse et de sa mise à disposition des autres "
"participants. Le Secrétariat du GDHCN peut apporter son aide pour la "
"coordination des questions opérationnelles et pratiques."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L151
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:151
msgid ""
"Each Participating country is REQUIRED to provide a list of one or more "
"Signing Certificate Authorities (SCAs) and a list of all valid Document "
"Signing Certificates (DSCs), and keep these lists current."
msgstr ""
"Il est OBLIGATOIRE que chaque pays participant fournisse une liste d’une ou "
"de plusieurs autorités de certification de signature (SCA) et une liste de "
"tous les certificats de signature de documents (DSC) valides, et tienne ces "
"listes à jour."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L1
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:1
msgid "Electronic Health Certificate Specification"
msgstr "Spécification des certificats sanitaires électroniques"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L40
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:40
msgid "Expiration Time (, claim key 4)"
msgstr "Date d’expiration (, clé de déclaration 4)"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L127
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:127
msgid ""
"For arbitrary data interfaces the HCERT container and its payloads may be "
"transferred as-is, utilising any underlying, 8 bit safe, reliable data "
"transport. These interfaces MAY include NFC, Bluetooth or transfer over an "
"application layer protocol, for example transfer of an HCERT from the Issuer"
" to a holder’s mobile device."
msgstr ""
"Pour des interfaces de données arbitraires, le conteneur HCERT et ses "
"charges utiles peuvent être transférés tels quels, au moyen de tout "
"transport de données sous-jacent fiable et compatible 8 bits. Ces interfaces"
" PEUVENT comprendre NFC, Bluetooth ou un transfert au moyen d’un protocole "
"de la couche application, par exemple le transfert d’un HCERT de l’émetteur "
"vers l’appareil mobile d’un titulaire."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L153
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:153
msgid "For the list of SCA certificates, each certificate:"
msgstr "Pour la liste des certificats SCA, chaque certificat :"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L229
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:229
msgid ""
"For the sake of simplicity: GDHCN Participants may both submit their "
"existing SCA certificates from their ICAO eMRTD systems or, as recommended "
"by the WHO, create one specifically for this health domain."
msgstr ""
"Par souci de simplicité : les participants au GDHCN peuvent soit soumettre "
"leurs certificats SCA existants issus de leurs systèmes eMRTD de l’ICAO, "
"soit, comme le recommande l’OMS, en créer un spécifiquement pour ce domaine "
"de la santé."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L56
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:56
msgid ""
"For this version of the specification, the SOG-IT set levels for the primary"
" and secondary algorithms are:"
msgstr ""
"Pour la présente version de la spécification, les niveaux fixés par SOG-IT "
"pour les algorithmes primaire et secondaire sont les suivants :"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L174
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:174
msgid ""
"GDHCN Participants can use a separate SCA (as per the WHO advice)(#ref) - "
"but may also submit their existing eMRT SCA and/or DSC certificates; and may"
" even choose to procure these from (commercial) trust centers - and submit "
"these. However, any DSC certificate must always be signed by the SCA "
"submitted by that country."
msgstr ""
"Les participants au GDHCN peuvent utiliser une SCA distincte (conformément à"
" l’avis de l’OMS)(#ref), mais peuvent également soumettre leurs certificats "
"SCA et/ou DSC eMRT existants ; ils peuvent même choisir de les obtenir "
"auprès de centres de confiance (commerciaux) et de les soumettre. Toutefois,"
" tout certificat DSC doit toujours être signé par la SCA soumise par le pays"
" concerné."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L225
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:225
msgid ""
"GDHCN Participants may also bilaterally exchange SCA certificates with a "
"number of other GDHCN Participants, verify these bilaterally and thus "
"compile their own lists of SCA and DSC certificates which is specific to "
"that GDHCN Participant. Verifiers may choose to rely on such a national "
"list."
msgstr ""
"Les participants au GDHCN peuvent également échanger des certificats SCA de "
"manière bilatérale avec un certain nombre d’autres participants au GDHCN, "
"les vérifier de manière bilatérale et compiler ainsi leurs propres listes de"
" certificats SCA et DSC, propres à ce participant au GDHCN. Les "
"vérificateurs peuvent choisir de s’appuyer sur une telle liste nationale."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L41
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:41
msgid ""
"Health Certificate (, claim key -260, see section 3.2.7 for subclaim details"
" )"
msgstr ""
"Certificat sanitaire (, clé de déclaration -260, voir la section 3.2.7 pour "
"le détail des sous-déclarations )"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L54
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:54
msgid ""
"However, it is essential and of utmost importance for the security of the "
"system that all implementations incorporate the secondary algorithm. For "
"this reason, both the primary and the secondary algorithm MUST be "
"implemented."
msgstr ""
"Toutefois, il est essentiel et de la plus haute importance pour la sécurité "
"du système que toutes les implémentations intègrent l’algorithme secondaire."
" Pour cette raison, l’algorithme primaire et l’algorithme secondaire DOIVENT"
" tous deux être mis en œuvre."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L203
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:203
msgid ""
"However, regardless of whether an Issuer decides to use HSMs or not, a key "
"roll-over schedule SHOULD be established where the frequency of the key "
"roll-overs is proportionate to the exposure of keys to external networks, "
"other systems and personnel. A well-chosen roll-over schedule also limits "
"the risks associated with erroneously issued health certificates, enabling "
"an Issuer to revoke such health certificates in batches, by withdrawing a "
"key, if required."
msgstr ""
"Toutefois, qu’un émetteur décide ou non d’utiliser des HSM, un calendrier de"
" renouvellement des clés DEVRAIT être établi, la fréquence des "
"renouvellements étant proportionnée à l’exposition des clés aux réseaux "
"externes, à d’autres systèmes et au personnel. Un calendrier de "
"renouvellement bien choisi limite également les risques liés aux certificats"
" sanitaires délivrés par erreur, en permettant à un émetteur de révoquer ces"
" certificats sanitaires par lots, en retirant une clé, si nécessaire."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L147
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:147
msgid ""
"If the optical code is printed on paper using low-resolution (< 300 dpi) "
"printers, care must be taken to represent each symbol (dot) of the QR code "
"exactly square. Non-proportional scaling will result in some rows or columns"
" in the QR having rectangular symbols, which will hamper readability in many"
" cases."
msgstr ""
"Si le code optique est imprimé sur papier au moyen d’imprimantes à basse "
"résolution (< 300 dpi), il convient de veiller à ce que chaque symbole "
"(point) du code QR soit représenté exactement carré. Une mise à l’échelle "
"non proportionnelle donnera lieu, dans certaines lignes ou colonnes du code "
"QR, à des symboles rectangulaires, ce qui nuira à la lisibilité dans de "
"nombreux cas."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L129
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:129
msgid ""
"If the transfer of the HCERT from the Issuer to the holder is based on a "
"presentation-only interface (e.g., SMS, e-mail), the Raw transport encoding "
"is obviously not applicable."
msgstr ""
"Si le transfert du HCERT de l’émetteur vers le titulaire repose sur une "
"interface de présentation uniquement (par exemple SMS, courrier "
"électronique), l’encodage de transport brut n’est de toute évidence pas "
"applicable."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L247
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:247
msgid ""
"In absence of any key usage extension (i.e. no extensions or zero "
"extensions), this certificate can be used to validate any type of HCERT.  "
"Other documents MAY define relevant additional extended key usage policy "
"identifiers used with validation of HCERTs."
msgstr ""
"En l’absence de toute extension d’utilisation de la clé (c’est-à-dire aucune"
" extension ou zéro extension), ce certificat peut être utilisé pour valider "
"tout type de HCERT.  D’autres documents PEUVENT définir des identifiants "
"supplémentaires pertinents de politique d’utilisation étendue de la clé "
"utilisés pour la validation des HCERT."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L159
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:159
msgid "In addition, for the list of DSC certificates, each certificate:"
msgstr "En outre, pour la liste des certificats DSC, chaque certificat :"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L121
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:121
msgid ""
"In an HCERT, claim key 5 holds the VHL payload as a CBOR map with text keys,"
" conforming to the Verifiable Health Link Payload logical model. A CBOR map "
"is used rather than a  URI string because the URI form base64url-encodes "
"JSON text inside the CBOR, which makes the QR code roughly a third larger."
msgstr ""
"Dans un HCERT, la clé de déclaration 5 contient la charge utile VHL sous la "
"forme d’un dictionnaire CBOR à clés textuelles, conforme au modèle logique "
"Verifiable Health Link Payload. Un dictionnaire CBOR est utilisé plutôt "
"qu’une chaîne d’URI  car la forme URI encode en base64url du texte JSON à "
"l’intérieur du CBOR, ce qui augmente la taille du code QR d’environ un "
"tiers."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L143
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:143
msgid ""
"In order for Verifiers to be able to detect the type of data encoded and to "
"select the proper decoding and processing scheme, the base45 encoded data "
"(as per this specification) SHALL be prefixed by the Context Identifier "
"string \"HC1:\". Future versions of this specification that impact "
"backwards-compatibility SHALL define a new Context Identifier, whereas the "
"character following \"HC\" SHALL be taken from the character set [1-9A-Z]. "
"The order of increments is defined to be in that order, i.e., first [1-9] "
"and then [A-Z]."
msgstr ""
"Afin que les vérificateurs puissent détecter le type de données encodées et "
"sélectionner le schéma de décodage et de traitement approprié, les données "
"encodées en base45 (conformément à la présente spécification) DOIVENT être "
"précédées de la chaîne d’identifiant de contexte \"HC1:\". Les futures "
"versions de la présente spécification ayant une incidence sur la "
"rétrocompatibilité DOIVENT définir un nouvel identifiant de contexte ; le "
"caractère suivant \"HC\" DOIT alors être choisi dans le jeu de caractères "
"[1-9A-Z]. L’ordre des incréments est défini comme suivant cet ordre, c’est-"
"à-dire d’abord [1-9], puis [A-Z]."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L139
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:139
msgid ""
"In order to better handle legacy equipment designed to operate on ASCII "
"payloads, the compressed CWT is encoded as ASCII using Base45 before being "
"encoded into a 2D barcode."
msgstr ""
"Afin de mieux prendre en charge les équipements existants conçus pour "
"fonctionner avec des charges utiles ASCII, le CWT compressé est encodé en "
"ASCII au moyen de Base45 avant d’être encodé dans un code-barres 2D."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L170
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:170
msgid ""
"Instead, the primary validity mechanism is the presence of the certificate "
"on the most recent version of that certificate list."
msgstr ""
"Le principal mécanisme de validité est plutôt la présence du certificat dans"
" la version la plus récente de cette liste de certificats."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L39
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:39
msgid "Issued At (, claim key 6)"
msgstr "Date de délivrance (, clé de déclaration 6)"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L38
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:38
msgid "Issuer (, claim key 1, optional, ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 of issuer)"
msgstr ""
"Émetteur (, clé de déclaration 1, facultatif, code ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 de "
"l’émetteur)"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L184
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:184
msgid ""
"It is anticipated that health certificates can not be reliably revoked once "
"issued, especially not if this specification would be used on a global "
"scale. Publishing of revocation information containing identifiers may also "
"create privacy concerns, as this information is per definition Personally "
"Identifiable Information (PII). For these reasons, this specification "
"requires the Issuer of HCERTs to limit the validity period of the signature "
"by specifying a signature expiry time. This requires the holder of a health "
"certificate to renew it at periodic intervals."
msgstr ""
"Il est prévu que les certificats sanitaires ne puissent pas être révoqués de"
" manière fiable une fois délivrés, surtout si la présente spécification "
"était utilisée à l’échelle mondiale. La publication d’informations de "
"révocation contenant des identifiants peut également soulever des "
"préoccupations en matière de protection de la vie privée, ces informations "
"étant par définition des informations permettant d’identifier une personne "
"(PII). Pour ces raisons, la présente spécification exige que l’émetteur de "
"HCERT limite la période de validité de la signature en précisant une date "
"d’expiration de la signature. Le titulaire d’un certificat sanitaire doit "
"donc le renouveler à intervalles réguliers."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L36
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:36
msgid "Key Identifier (, label 4)"
msgstr "Identifiant de clé (, étiquette 4)"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L161
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:161
msgid ""
"MUST be signed with the private key corresponding to a SCA certificate "
"published on the aforementioned list."
msgstr ""
"DOIT être signé avec la clé privée correspondant à un certificat SCA publié "
"sur la liste susmentionnée."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L157
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:157
msgid ""
"MUST contain a unique Subject Key Identifier (SKI) according to (RFC5280)."
msgstr ""
"DOIT contenir un identifiant de clé du sujet (SKI) unique conformément à "
"(RFC5280)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L155
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:155
msgid ""
"MUST contain a valid Country attribute in the subject DN that matches the "
"country of issuance."
msgstr ""
"DOIT contenir un attribut Country valide dans le DN du sujet, correspondant "
"au pays de délivrance."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L162
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:162
msgid ""
"MUST contain an Authority Key Identifier (AKI) matching the Subject Key "
"Identifier (SKI) of the issuing SCA certificate."
msgstr ""
"DOIT contenir un identifiant de clé de l’autorité (AKI) correspondant à "
"l’identifiant de clé du sujet (SKI) du certificat SCA émetteur."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L156
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:156
msgid "MUST contain DN that is unique within the specified country."
msgstr "DOIT contenir un DN unique au sein du pays spécifié."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L163
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:163
msgid ""
"MUST have a validity period that is in line with or longer than the validity"
" period of all certificates signed using that key."
msgstr ""
"DOIT avoir une période de validité conforme ou supérieure à la période de "
"validité de tous les certificats signés au moyen de cette clé."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L94
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:94
msgid ""
"Note here that the JSON is purely for schema purposes. The wire format is "
"CBOR as defined in (RFC 7049). Application developers may not actually ever "
"decode or encode to and from the JSON format, but use the in-memory "
"structure."
msgstr ""
"Il convient de noter ici que le JSON n’est utilisé qu’à des fins de schéma. "
"Le format de transmission est CBOR, tel que défini dans (RFC 7049). Les "
"développeurs d’applications peuvent en réalité ne jamais décoder ou encoder "
"vers et depuis le format JSON, mais utiliser la structure en mémoire."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L235
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:235
msgid ""
"Note that Verifiers do not need to calculate the  based on the DSC "
"certificate and can directly match the Key Identifier in issued health "
"certificates with the  on the trusted list."
msgstr ""
"Il convient de noter que les vérificateurs n’ont pas besoin de calculer le  "
"à partir du certificat DSC et peuvent directement faire correspondre "
"l’identifiant de clé figurant dans les certificats sanitaires délivrés avec "
"le  figurant sur la liste de confiance."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L241
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:241
msgid "OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.1847.2021.1.1 --  valid for test"
msgstr "OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.1847.2021.1.1 --  valide pour les tests"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L242
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:242
msgid "OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.1847.2021.1.2  -- valid for vaccinations"
msgstr "OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.1847.2021.1.2  -- valide pour les vaccinations"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L243
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:243
msgid "OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.1847.2021.1.3  -- valid for recovery"
msgstr "OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.1847.2021.1.3  -- valide pour la guérison"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L52
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:52
msgid ""
"One primary and one secondary algorithm is defined. The secondary algorithm "
"should only be used if the primary algorithm is not acceptable within the "
"rules and regulations imposed on the implementer."
msgstr ""
"Un algorithme primaire et un algorithme secondaire sont définis. "
"L’algorithme secondaire ne devrait être utilisé que si l’algorithme primaire"
" n’est pas acceptable au regard des règles et réglementations imposées au "
"responsable de la mise en œuvre."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L14
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:14
msgid ""
"Organisations adopting this specification for issuing health certificates "
"are called Issuers and organisations accepting health certificates as proof "
"of health status are called Verifiers. Together, these are called "
"Participants. Some aspects in this document must be coordinated between the "
"Participants, such as the management of a namespace and the distribution of "
"cryptographic keys. It is assumed that a party, hereafter referred to as the"
" Secretariat, carries out these tasks. The health certificate container "
"format (HCERT) of this specification is generic, but in this context used to"
" carry the WHO Digital Covid Certificate (DCC)."
msgstr ""
"Les organisations qui adoptent la présente spécification pour délivrer des "
"certificats sanitaires sont appelées émetteurs, et les organisations qui "
"acceptent des certificats sanitaires comme preuve de l’état de santé sont "
"appelées vérificateurs. Ensemble, elles sont appelées participants. Certains"
" aspects du présent document doivent être coordonnés entre les participants,"
" tels que la gestion d’un espace de noms et la distribution des clés "
"cryptographiques. Il est présumé qu’une partie, ci-après dénommée le "
"Secrétariat, accomplit ces tâches. Le format de conteneur des certificats "
"sanitaires (HCERT) de la présente spécification est générique, mais il est "
"utilisé dans ce contexte pour transporter le certificat COVID numérique "
"(DCC) de l’OMS."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L37
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:37
msgid "Payload"
msgstr "Charge utile"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L58
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:58
msgid ""
"Primary Algorithm: The primary algorithm is Elliptic Curve Digital Signature"
" Algorithm (ECDSA) as defined in (ISO/IEC 14888–3:2006) section 2.3, using "
"the P–256 parameters as defined in appendix D (D.1.2.3) of (FIPS PUB 186–4) "
"in combination with the SHA–256 hash algorithm as defined in (ISO/IEC "
"10118–3:2004) function 4."
msgstr ""
"Algorithme primaire : l’algorithme primaire est l’algorithme de signature "
"numérique à courbe elliptique (ECDSA) tel que défini dans (ISO/IEC "
"14888–3:2006), section 2.3, utilisant les paramètres P–256 tels que définis "
"à l’appendice D (D.1.2.3) de (FIPS PUB 186–4), en combinaison avec "
"l’algorithme de hachage SHA–256 tel que défini dans (ISO/IEC 10118–3:2004), "
"fonction 4."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L34
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:34
msgid "Protected Header"
msgstr "En-tête protégé"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L62
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:62
msgid ""
"Secondary Algorithm: The secondary algorithm is RSASSA-PSS as defined in "
"(RFC 8230) with a modulus of 2048 bits in combination with the SHA–256 hash "
"algorithm as defined in (ISO/IEC 10118–3:2004) function 4."
msgstr ""
"Algorithme secondaire : l’algorithme secondaire est RSASSA-PSS tel que "
"défini dans (RFC 8230), avec un module de 2048 bits, en combinaison avec "
"l’algorithme de hachage SHA–256 tel que défini dans (ISO/IEC 10118–3:2004), "
"fonction 4."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L164
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:164
msgid ""
"SHOULD contain a unique Subject Key Identifier derived from the subject "
"public key."
msgstr ""
"DEVRAIT contenir un identifiant de clé du sujet unique dérivé de la clé "
"publique du sujet."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L42
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:42
msgid "Signature"
msgstr "Signature"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L35
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:35
msgid "Signature Algorithm (, label 1)"
msgstr "Algorithme de signature (, étiquette 1)"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L98
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:98
msgid ""
"Strings in the JSON object SHOULD be NFC normalised according to the Unicode"
" standard. Decoding applications SHOULD however be permissive and robust in "
"these aspects, and acceptance of any reasonable type conversion is strongly "
"encouraged. If non-normalised data is found during decoding, or in "
"subsequent comparison functions, implementations SHOULD behave as if the "
"input is normalised to NFC."
msgstr ""
"Les chaînes de l’objet JSON DEVRAIENT être normalisées selon la forme NFC "
"conformément à la norme Unicode. Les applications de décodage DEVRAIENT "
"toutefois être permissives et robustes à cet égard, et l’acceptation de "
"toute conversion de type raisonnable est vivement encouragée. Si des données"
" non normalisées sont détectées lors du décodage ou dans des fonctions de "
"comparaison ultérieures, les implémentations DEVRAIENT se comporter comme si"
" l’entrée était normalisée selon la forme NFC."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L101
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:101
msgid ""
"subclaims 0 and above are reserved by WHO to be assigned, a new sub claim "
"can be requested for by requesting to create a new trust domain"
msgstr ""
"les sous-déclarations 0 et supérieures sont réservées à l’OMS, qui les "
"attribue ; une nouvelle sous-déclaration peut être demandée en sollicitant "
"la création d’un nouveau domaine de confiance"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L102
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:102
msgid ""
"subclaims for negative integer values are for development purposes and are "
"free to use"
msgstr ""
"les sous-déclarations à valeurs entières négatives sont destinées au "
"développement et peuvent être utilisées librement"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L227
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:227
msgid ""
"Such GDHCN Participant-specific lists are expected to be adapted in the "
"format for their own national setting. As such, the file format of this "
"trusted list may vary, e.g., it can be a signed JWKS (JWK set format per RFC"
" 7517 section 5) or any other format specific to the technology used in that"
" GDHCN Participant."
msgstr ""
"Il est prévu que le format de ces listes propres à chaque participant au "
"GDHCN soit adapté au contexte national de chacun. Ainsi, le format de "
"fichier de cette liste de confiance peut varier ; il peut par exemple s’agir"
" d’un JWKS signé (format d’ensemble JWK selon la RFC 7517, section 5) ou de "
"tout autre format propre à la technologie utilisée par ce participant au "
"GDHCN."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L215
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:215
msgid ""
"The \"GDHCN Secretariat\" is a functional role; not a person or a piece of "
"software. It is expected that the WHO’s GDHCN Trust Network Gateway will "
"automate most of these tasks."
msgstr ""
"Le « Secrétariat du GDHCN » est un rôle fonctionnel, et non une personne ou "
"un logiciel. Il est prévu que la passerelle du réseau de confiance du GDHCN "
"de l’OMS automatise la plupart de ces tâches."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L186
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:186
msgid ""
"The acceptable validity period may be determined by practical constraints. "
"For example, a traveler may not have the possibility to renew the health "
"certificate during a trip overseas. However, it may also be the case that an"
" Issuer is considering the possibility of a security compromise of some "
"sort, which requires the Issuer to withdraw an DSC (invalidating all health "
"certificates issued using that key which are still within their validity "
"period). The consequences of such an event may be limited by regularly "
"rolling Issuer keys and requiring renewal of all health certificates, on "
"some reasonable interval."
msgstr ""
"La période de validité acceptable peut être déterminée par des contraintes "
"pratiques. Par exemple, un voyageur peut ne pas avoir la possibilité de "
"renouveler son certificat sanitaire au cours d’un voyage à l’étranger. "
"Toutefois, il se peut également qu’un émetteur envisage la possibilité d’une"
" compromission de la sécurité d’un type ou d’un autre, qui l’obligerait à "
"retirer un DSC (invalidant ainsi tous les certificats sanitaires délivrés au"
" moyen de cette clé qui sont encore dans leur période de validité). Les "
"conséquences d’un tel événement peuvent être limitées par un renouvellement "
"régulier des clés de l’émetteur et en exigeant le renouvellement de tous les"
" certificats sanitaires à intervalle raisonnable."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L96
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:96
msgid "The Claim Key to be used to identify this claim is -260."
msgstr ""
"La clé de déclaration à utiliser pour identifier cette déclaration est -260."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L192
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:192
msgid ""
"The confidentiality of cryptographic keys can be compromised in a number of "
"different ways, for instance:"
msgstr ""
"La confidentialité des clés cryptographiques peut être compromise de "
"différentes manières, par exemple :"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L239
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:239
msgid ""
"The document signing certificate MAY contain Extended Key Usage extension "
"fields; these being:"
msgstr ""
"Le certificat de signature de documents PEUT contenir des champs d’extension"
" d’utilisation étendue de la clé, à savoir :"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L245
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:245
msgid ""
"The DSC may contain an extended key usage extension with zero or more key "
"usage policy identifiers that constrain the types of HCERTs this certificate"
" is allowed to verify. If one or more are present, the verifiers SHALL "
"verify the key usage against the stored HCERT."
msgstr ""
"Le DSC peut contenir une extension d’utilisation étendue de la clé "
"comportant zéro ou plusieurs identifiants de politique d’utilisation de la "
"clé, qui restreignent les types de HCERT que ce certificat est autorisé à "
"vérifier. Si un ou plusieurs identifiants sont présents, les vérificateurs "
"DOIVENT vérifier l’utilisation de la clé par rapport au HCERT stocké."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L22
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:22
msgid ""
"The Electronic Health Certificate Container Format (HCERT) is designed to "
"provide a uniform and standardised vehicle for health certificates from "
"different Issuers. The aim is to harmonise how these health certificates are"
" represented, encoded and signed with the goal of facilitating "
"interoperability."
msgstr ""
"Le format de conteneur des certificats sanitaires électroniques (HCERT) est "
"conçu pour fournir un vecteur uniforme et normalisé pour les certificats "
"sanitaires provenant de différents émetteurs. L’objectif est d’harmoniser la"
" manière dont ces certificats sanitaires sont représentés, encodés et "
"signés, afin de faciliter l’interopérabilité."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L78
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:78
msgid ""
"The Expiration Time () claim SHALL hold a timestamp in the integer "
"NumericDate format (as specified in RFC 8392 section 2) indicating for how "
"long this particular signature over the Payload SHALL be considered valid, "
"after which a Verifier MUST reject the Payload as expired. The purpose of "
"the expiry parameter is to force a limit of the validity period of the "
"health certificate. The Claim Key 4 is used to identify this claim."
msgstr ""
"La déclaration Date d’expiration () DOIT contenir un horodatage au format "
"entier NumericDate (tel que spécifié dans la RFC 8392, section 2) indiquant "
"pendant combien de temps cette signature particulière de la charge utile "
"DOIT être considérée comme valide, après quoi un vérificateur DOIT rejeter "
"la charge utile comme expirée. Le paramètre d’expiration a pour objet "
"d’imposer une limite à la période de validité du certificat sanitaire. La "
"clé de déclaration 4 est utilisée pour identifier cette déclaration."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L80
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:80
msgid "The Expiration Time MUST not exceed the validity period of the DSC."
msgstr ""
"La date d’expiration NE DOIT PAS dépasser la période de validité du DSC."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L219
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:219
msgid ""
"The GDHCN Participant certificates are called Signer Certificate Authorities"
" (SCAs) and are  self-signed certificates. Participants may have more than "
"one (e.g., in case of regional devolution). These SCAs regularly sign the "
"Document Signing Certificates (DSCs) used for signing HCERTs. GDHCN "
"Participants will each maintain a public register of the DSC certificates "
"kept current, communicated to the WHO’s Secretariat and published at a "
"stable URL for bilateral exchange. GDHCN Participants MUST remove any "
"revoked or stale certificates from this list."
msgstr ""
"Les certificats des participants au GDHCN sont appelés autorités de "
"certification de signataire (SCA) et sont des certificats  auto-signés. Les "
"participants peuvent en avoir plusieurs (par exemple en cas de "
"décentralisation régionale). Ces SCA signent régulièrement les certificats "
"de signature de documents (DSC) utilisés pour signer les HCERT. Chaque "
"participant au GDHCN tiendra à jour un registre public des certificats DSC, "
"communiqué au Secrétariat de l’OMS et publié à une URL stable en vue d’un "
"échange bilatéral. Les participants au GDHCN DOIVENT retirer de cette liste "
"tout certificat révoqué ou obsolète."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L211
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:211
msgid ""
"The HCERT signature verification process necessitates the use of a public "
"key. GDHCN Participants, or institutions within these participants, are "
"responsible for providing these public keys. Ultimately, every Verifier "
"needs to have a list of all public keys it is willing to trust (as the "
"public key is not part of the HCERT)."
msgstr ""
"Le processus de vérification de la signature HCERT nécessite l’utilisation "
"d’une clé publique. Les participants au GDHCN, ou les institutions relevant "
"de ces participants, sont chargés de fournir ces clés publiques. En "
"définitive, chaque vérificateur doit disposer d’une liste de toutes les clés"
" publiques auxquelles il est disposé à faire confiance (la clé publique ne "
"faisant pas partie du HCERT)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L92
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:92
msgid ""
"The Health Certificate () claim is a JSON (RFC 7159) object containing the "
"health status information. The actual wire format of HCERT is content "
"neutral. Several different types of health certificate MAY exist under the "
"same claim, of which the European DCC is one."
msgstr ""
"La déclaration Certificat sanitaire () est un objet JSON (RFC 7159) "
"contenant les informations sur l’état de santé. Le format de transmission "
"effectif du HCERT est neutre quant au contenu. Plusieurs types différents de"
" certificats sanitaires PEUVENT exister sous la même déclaration, dont le "
"DCC européen."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L28
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:28
msgid ""
"The integrity and authenticity of origin of payload data MUST be verifiable "
"by the Verifier. To provide this mechanism, the issuer MUST sign the CWT "
"using an asymmetric electronic signature scheme as defined in the COSE "
"specification (RFC 8152)."
msgstr ""
"L’intégrité et l’authenticité de l’origine des données de la charge utile "
"DOIVENT pouvoir être vérifiées par le vérificateur. Pour fournir ce "
"mécanisme, l’émetteur DOIT signer le CWT au moyen d’un schéma de signature "
"électronique asymétrique tel que défini dans la spécification COSE (RFC "
"8152)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L84
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:84
msgid ""
"The Issued At () claim SHALL hold a timestamp in the integer NumericDate "
"format (as specified in RFC 8392 section 2) indicating the time when the "
"health certificate was created."
msgstr ""
"La déclaration Date de délivrance () DOIT contenir un horodatage au format "
"entier NumericDate (tel que spécifié dans la RFC 8392, section 2) indiquant "
"la date et l’heure de création du certificat sanitaire."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L86
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:86
msgid "The Issued At field MUST not predate the validity period of the DSC."
msgstr ""
"Le champ Date de délivrance NE DOIT PAS être antérieur à la période de "
"validité du DSC."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L74
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:74
msgid ""
"The Issuer () claim is a string value that MAY optionally hold the ISO "
"3166-1 alpha-2 Country Code of the entity issuing the health certificate. "
"This claim can be used by a Verifier to identify which set of DSCs to use "
"for validation. The Claim Key 1 is used to identify this claim."
msgstr ""
"La déclaration Émetteur () est une valeur de chaîne qui PEUT, à titre "
"facultatif, contenir le code de pays ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 de l’entité qui "
"délivre le certificat sanitaire. Cette déclaration peut être utilisée par un"
" vérificateur pour déterminer quel ensemble de DSC utiliser pour la "
"validation. La clé de déclaration 1 est utilisée pour identifier cette "
"déclaration."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L194
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:194
msgid "The key generation process may be flawed, resulting in weak keys."
msgstr ""
"Le processus de génération des clés peut être défaillant et produire des "
"clés faibles."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L68
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:68
msgid ""
"The Key Identifier () claim is used by Verifiers for selecting the correct "
"public key from a list of keys pertaining to the Issuer () Claim. Several "
"keys may be used in parallel by an Issuer for administrative reasons and "
"when performing key rollovers. The Key Identifier is not a security-critical"
" field. For this reason, it MAY also be placed in an unprotected header if "
"required. Verifiers MUST accept both options.  If both options are present, "
"the Key Identifier in the protected header MUST be used."
msgstr ""
"La déclaration Identifiant de clé () est utilisée par les vérificateurs pour"
" sélectionner la clé publique correcte dans une liste de clés relevant de la"
" déclaration Émetteur (). Plusieurs clés peuvent être utilisées en parallèle"
" par un émetteur pour des raisons administratives et lors des "
"renouvellements de clés. L’identifiant de clé n’est pas un champ critique "
"pour la sécurité. Pour cette raison, il PEUT également être placé dans un "
"en-tête non protégé si nécessaire. Les vérificateurs DOIVENT accepter les "
"deux options.  Si les deux options sont présentes, l’identifiant de clé "
"figurant dans l’en-tête protégé DOIT être utilisé."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L233
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:233
msgid ""
"The Key Identifier () is calculated when constructing the list of trusted "
"public keys from DSC certificates and consists of a truncated (first 8 "
"bytes) SHA-256 fingerprint of the DSC encoded in DER (raw) format."
msgstr ""
"L’identifiant de clé () est calculé lors de la constitution de la liste des "
"clés publiques de confiance à partir des certificats DSC et consiste en une "
"empreinte SHA-256 tronquée (8 premiers octets) du DSC encodé au format DER "
"(brut)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L197
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:197
msgid "The keys may be calculated using cryptanalysis."
msgstr "Les clés peuvent être calculées par cryptanalyse."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L195
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:195
msgid "The keys may be exposed by human error."
msgstr "Les clés peuvent être exposées à la suite d’une erreur humaine."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L196
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:196
msgid "The keys may be stolen by external or internal perpetrators."
msgstr "Les clés peuvent être volées par des auteurs externes ou internes."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L46
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:46
msgid "The logical model can be found specified here"
msgstr "Le modèle logique est spécifié ici"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L145
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:145
msgid ""
"The optical code is RECOMMENDED to be rendered on the presentation media "
"with a diagonal size between 35 mm and 60 mm to accommodate readers with "
"fixed optics where the presentation media is required to be placed on the "
"surface of the reader."
msgstr ""
"Il est RECOMMANDÉ que le code optique soit restitué sur le support de "
"présentation avec une diagonale comprise entre 35 mm et 60 mm, afin de "
"convenir aux lecteurs à optique fixe pour lesquels le support de "
"présentation doit être placé sur la surface du lecteur."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L201
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:201
msgid ""
"The other risks mentioned here are related to the Issuers' operating "
"environments. One effective control to mitigate significant parts of these "
"risks is to generate, store and use the private keys in Hardware Security "
"Modules (HSMs). Use of HSMs for signing health certificates is highly "
"encouraged."
msgstr ""
"Les autres risques mentionnés ici sont liés aux environnements "
"d’exploitation des émetteurs. Une mesure de contrôle efficace pour atténuer "
"une part importante de ces risques consiste à générer, stocker et utiliser "
"les clés privées dans des modules de sécurité matériels (HSM). L’utilisation"
" de HSM pour la signature des certificats sanitaires est vivement "
"encouragée."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L26
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:26
msgid ""
"The payload is structured and encoded as a CBOR with a COSE digital "
"signature. This is commonly known as a \"CBOR Web Token\" (CWT), and is "
"defined in RFC 8392. The payload, as defined below, is transported in a  "
"claim."
msgstr ""
"La charge utile est structurée et encodée en CBOR avec une signature "
"numérique COSE. Cette structure est communément appelée « CBOR Web Token » "
"(CWT) et est définie dans la RFC 8392. La charge utile, telle que définie "
"ci-dessous, est transportée dans une déclaration ."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L16
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:16
msgid ""
"The Public Key Infrastructure (PKI) that underpins the trust model consists "
"of a Signing Certificate Authority (SCA) certificate which is used to issue "
"(i.e. sign) the Document Signing Certificate (DSC). The DSC is then used to "
"sign the DCC. The acronyms \"PKI\", \"SCA\" and \"DSC\" are used in the "
"context of the document to refer to the aforementioned concepts."
msgstr ""
"L’infrastructure à clés publiques (PKI) qui sous-tend le modèle de confiance"
" se compose d’un certificat d’autorité de certification de signature (SCA), "
"utilisé pour émettre (c’est-à-dire signer) le certificat de signature de "
"documents (DSC). Le DSC est ensuite utilisé pour signer le DCC. Les "
"acronymes « PKI », « SCA » et « DSC » sont utilisés dans le présent document"
" pour désigner les concepts susmentionnés."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L141
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:141
msgid ""
"The QR format as defined in (ISO/IEC 18004:2015) SHALL be used for 2D "
"barcode generation. An error correction rate of ‘Q’ (around 25%) is "
"RECOMMENDED.  The Alphanumeric (Mode 2/QR Code symbols 0010) MUST be used in"
" conjunction with Base45."
msgstr ""
"Le format QR tel que défini dans (ISO/IEC 18004:2015) DOIT être utilisé pour"
" la génération de codes-barres 2D. Un taux de correction d’erreurs de « Q » "
"(environ 25 %) est RECOMMANDÉ.  Le mode alphanumérique (Mode 2/symboles de "
"code QR 0010) DOIT être utilisé conjointement avec Base45."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L223
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:223
msgid ""
"The resulting list of DSC certificates then provides the aggregated set of "
"acceptable public keys (and the corresponding s) that Verifiers can use to "
"validate the signatures over the HCERTs. Verifiers MUST fetch and update "
"this list regularly."
msgstr ""
"La liste de certificats DSC qui en résulte fournit alors l’ensemble agrégé "
"des clés publiques acceptables (et des s correspondants) que les "
"vérificateurs peuvent utiliser pour valider les signatures des HCERT. Les "
"vérificateurs DOIVENT récupérer et mettre à jour cette liste régulièrement."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L221
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:221
msgid ""
"The Secretariat will regularly aggregate and publish the GDHCN Participants "
"DSCs, after having verified these against the list of SCA certificates "
"(which have been conveyed and verified by other means)."
msgstr ""
"Le Secrétariat agrégera et publiera régulièrement les DSC des participants "
"au GDHCN, après les avoir vérifiés par rapport à la liste des certificats "
"SCA (qui ont été transmis et vérifiés par d’autres moyens)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L50
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:50
msgid ""
"The Signature Algorithm () parameter indicates what algorithm is used for "
"creating the signature. It must meet or exceed current SOG-IT guidelines."
msgstr ""
"Le paramètre Algorithme de signature () indique l’algorithme utilisé pour "
"créer la signature. Il doit satisfaire ou dépasser les lignes directrices "
"SOG-IT en vigueur."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L44
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:44
msgid ""
"The Signature is required to be sent in the CWT and MUST accompany the "
"payload for validation."
msgstr ""
"La signature doit obligatoirement être transmise dans le CWT et DOIT "
"accompagner la charge utile aux fins de la validation."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L217
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:217
msgid ""
"The system consists of two layers; for each GDHCN Participant one or more "
"country level certificates that each signs one or more document signing "
"certificates that are used in day to day operations."
msgstr ""
"Le système se compose de deux niveaux : pour chaque participant au GDHCN, un"
" ou plusieurs certificats au niveau du pays, qui signent chacun un ou "
"plusieurs certificats de signature de documents utilisés dans les opérations"
" courantes."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L60
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:60
msgid "This corresponds to the COSE algorithm parameter ."
msgstr "Cela correspond au paramètre d’algorithme COSE ."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L64
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:64
msgid "This corresponds to the COSE algorithm parameter: ."
msgstr "Cela correspond au paramètre d’algorithme COSE : ."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L10
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:10
msgid ""
"This document specifies a generic data structure and encoding mechanisms for"
" electronic health certificates. It also specifies a transport encoding "
"mechanism in a machine-readable optical format (QR), which can be displayed "
"on the screen of a mobile device or printed on a piece of paper."
msgstr ""
"Le présent document spécifie une structure de données générique et des "
"mécanismes d’encodage pour les certificats sanitaires électroniques. Il "
"spécifie également un mécanisme d’encodage de transport dans un format "
"optique lisible par machine (QR), qui peut être affiché sur l’écran d’un "
"appareil mobile ou imprimé sur une feuille de papier."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L207
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:207
msgid ""
"This specification may be used in a way that implies receiving data from "
"untrusted sources into systems that may be of mission-critical nature. To "
"minimise the risks associated with this attack vector, all input fields MUST"
" be properly validated by data types, lengths and contents. The Issuer "
"Signature SHALL also be verified before any processing of the contents of "
"the HCERT takes place. However, the validation of the Issuer Signature "
"implies parsing the Protected Issuer Header first, in which a potential "
"attacker may attempt to inject carefully crafted information designed to "
"compromise the security of the system."
msgstr ""
"La présente spécification peut être utilisée d’une manière qui implique la "
"réception, dans des systèmes susceptibles d’être critiques, de données "
"provenant de sources non fiables. Afin de réduire au minimum les risques "
"liés à ce vecteur d’attaque, tous les champs d’entrée DOIVENT être "
"correctement validés en fonction des types de données, des longueurs et des "
"contenus. La signature de l’émetteur DOIT également être vérifiée avant tout"
" traitement du contenu du HCERT. Toutefois, la validation de la signature de"
" l’émetteur implique d’analyser d’abord l’en-tête protégé de l’émetteur, "
"dans lequel un attaquant potentiel peut tenter d’injecter des informations "
"soigneusement élaborées en vue de compromettre la sécurité du système."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L190
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:190
msgid ""
"This specification relies heavily on strong cryptographic mechanisms to "
"secure data integrity and data origin authentication. Maintaining the "
"confidentiality of the private keys is therefore of utmost importance."
msgstr ""
"La présente spécification repose largement sur des mécanismes "
"cryptographiques robustes pour garantir l’intégrité des données et "
"l’authentification de l’origine des données. Le maintien de la "
"confidentialité des clés privées est donc de la plus haute importance."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L6
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:6
msgid ""
"This specification, originally developed by the European Union (EU), is "
"based on the EU Digital Covid Certificate (EU DCC) project by the European "
"eHealth network. The specification is now under the maintenance of the WHO "
"from January 1, 2024. The WHO oversees all updates and modifications to "
"HCERT claims. GDHCN Participants may propose additional claims or "
"modifications through the WHO’s GDHCN Secretariat, ensuring the framework "
"remains responsive and adaptable to evolving global health needs."
msgstr ""
"La présente spécification, élaborée à l’origine par l’Union européenne (UE),"
" est fondée sur le projet de certificat COVID numérique de l’UE (EU DCC) du "
"réseau européen « santé en ligne » (eHealth Network). Depuis le 1er janvier "
"2024, la spécification est maintenue par l’OMS. L’OMS supervise toutes les "
"mises à jour et modifications des déclarations HCERT. Les participants au "
"GDHCN peuvent proposer des déclarations supplémentaires ou des modifications"
" par l’intermédiaire du Secrétariat du GDHCN de l’OMS, ce qui permet au "
"cadre de rester réactif et adaptable à l’évolution des besoins de santé "
"mondiaux."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L135
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:135
msgid ""
"To lower size and to improve speed and reliability in the reading process of"
" the HCERT, the CWT SHALL be compressed using ZLIB (RFC 1950) and the "
"Deflate compression mechanism in the format defined in (RFC 1951)."
msgstr ""
"Afin de réduire la taille et d’améliorer la rapidité et la fiabilité de la "
"lecture du HCERT, le CWT DOIT être compressé au moyen de ZLIB (RFC 1950) et "
"du mécanisme de compression Deflate dans le format défini dans (RFC 1951)."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L199
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:199
msgid ""
"To mitigate against the risks that the signing algorithm is found to be "
"weak, allowing the private keys to be compromised through cryptanalysis, "
"this specification recommends all Participants to implement a secondary "
"fallback signature algorithm based on different parameters or a different "
"mathematical problem than the primary."
msgstr ""
"Afin d’atténuer le risque que l’algorithme de signature se révèle faible, "
"permettant la compromission des clés privées par cryptanalyse, la présente "
"spécification recommande à tous les participants de mettre en œuvre un "
"algorithme de signature secondaire de repli fondé sur des paramètres "
"différents ou sur un problème mathématique différent de celui de "
"l’algorithme primaire."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L88
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:88
msgid ""
"Verifiers MAY apply additional policies with the purpose of restricting the "
"validity of the health certificate based on the time of issue. The Claim Key"
" 6 is used to identify this claim."
msgstr ""
"Les vérificateurs PEUVENT appliquer des politiques supplémentaires visant à "
"restreindre la validité du certificat sanitaire en fonction de la date de "
"délivrance. La clé de déclaration 6 est utilisée pour identifier cette "
"déclaration."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L3
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:3
msgid "Version 1.1.1, 2024-02-27"
msgstr "Version 1.1.1, 2024-02-27"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L178
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:178
msgid ""
"When designing a scheme using this specification, several important security"
" aspects must be considered. These cannot preemptively be accounted for in "
"this specification but must be identified, analysed and monitored by the "
"Participants."
msgstr ""
"Lors de la conception d’un système fondé sur la présente spécification, "
"plusieurs aspects de sécurité importants doivent être pris en considération."
" Ceux-ci ne peuvent pas être pris en compte à l’avance dans la présente "
"spécification, mais doivent être identifiés, analysés et surveillés par les "
"participants."

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md#L103
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/hcert_spec.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/hcert_spec.html
#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:103
msgid ""
"While the logical model enlists assigned sub claims, the ones listed in this"
" specification are considered authoritative"
msgstr ""
"Bien que le modèle logique énumère les sous-déclarations attribuées, celles "
"qui figurent dans la présente spécification sont considérées comme faisant "
"foi"

